# When to call Headroom

`headroom_compress` / `headroom_retrieve` / `headroom_stats` are on-demand. They do not run after every prompt. RTK already rewrites Shell tool output.

Call `headroom_compress` only when a tool result or pasted blob is large enough to waste context (roughly thousands of tokens): long logs, fat search/crawl dumps, huge file reads, big JSON.

Do **not** call Headroom for ordinary edits — code or not (docs, Nix, Copier, commit messages, short files).

```
# ❌ BAD — compress a 20-line docs tweak or a one-hunk Nix change
# ✅ GOOD — compress a 5k-line test log or a full-repo ripgrep dump, then keep working
```

Call `headroom_retrieve` only after a successful `headroom_compress`, using that response’s `hash`. Use it when the compressed text is not enough (a specific error line, a file path, a JSON field). Optional `query` searches inside the original. Local MCP originals expire after about an hour. Do not invent hashes. Do not retrieve “just in case.”

`headroom_stats` is optional, for checking savings — not part of the edit loop.
